IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- the Thirteenth Schedule -- criteria for a small company and a small group (the meanings s 205C(5) hands to it). LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- THE SHAPE. A company (or group) is small from a financial year if it qualifies under paragraph 2, 3 or 4 (7, 8 or 9 for a group), and it
-- then stays small until it ceases under paragraph 5 (10) (paragraph 1, paragraph 13). The history is carried by ONE input, the status of
-- the immediately preceding financial year, so that a person states the facts of one year at a time; a chain of years is tested in
-- sgc2-tests-sch13.l4 (paragraph 14: a company that ceased may qualify again).
--
-- THE FIGURES. $10 million and 50 employees are the Schedule's own numbers and are written here, not asked. Revenue and total assets are
-- in Singapore dollars. "Does not exceed $10 million" is AT MOST 10,000,000; "not more than 50 employees" is AT MOST 50.
--
-- TWO READINGS the text leaves open, each coded (fork lines F-S1 and F-S2 in NOTES.md):
--   (A) "satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 financial years": in EACH of the two years at least 2 of the 3
--       criteria hold (the two need not be the same in both years). The functions use (A). The other reading (B), the SAME two
--       criteria in both years, is `sch 13 para 2(b) ... (other reading)` and is not called by any other function.
--   (C1) "does not satisfy any 2 of the criteria for each of the 2 consecutive financial years": in EACH of the two years fewer than 2
--       criteria hold, so a company that fails in only one of the two years does not cease. The functions use (C1). The other reading (C2),
--       failing in EITHER year, is `sch 13 para 5(b) ... (other reading)` and is not called by any other function.
--
-- The ordinal of a financial year ("the first, second, third financial year after incorporation") is asked as a number, not worked out
-- from dates (the Schedule does not say how the first financial year is fixed; fork line F-S3).

§ `The Schedule's own figures and the one date it names`

-- Paragraph 2(b)(i) and (ii): $10 million; (iii): not more than 50 employees. (The same figures recur in paragraphs 3, 4, 5 and 7 to 10.)
`sch 13 the ceiling for revenue and for total assets, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 10000000

`sch 13 the ceiling for employees` MEANS 50

`sch 13 the day 1 July 2015` MEANS Date 1 7 2015

-- One financial year's figures, of a company or (consolidated, aggregate) of a group.
DECLARE `sch 13 year figures` HAS
    `sch 13 the revenue for the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 13 the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 13 the number of employees at the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER

§ `Paragraph 2(b): the three criteria and "any 2" of them`

-- src:29035 | (b) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 financial
-- src:29036 | years immediately preceding the financial year:
-- src:29038 | (i) the revenue of the company for each financial year does not
-- src:29039 | exceed $10 million;
-- src:29041 | (ii) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of each
-- src:29042 | financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29044 | (iii) it has at the end of each financial year not more than
-- src:29045 | 50 employees.
@ref sch 13 para 2(b) (src:29035-29045)
GIVEN figures IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` MEANS
    figures's `sch 13 the revenue for the financial year, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST `sch 13 the ceiling for revenue and for total assets, in Singapore dollars`

@ref sch 13 para 2(b) (src:29035-29045)
GIVEN figures IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` MEANS
    figures's `sch 13 the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST `sch 13 the ceiling for revenue and for total assets, in Singapore dollars`

@ref sch 13 para 2(b) (src:29035-29045)
GIVEN figures IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` MEANS
    figures's `sch 13 the number of employees at the end of the financial year` AT MOST `sch 13 the ceiling for employees`

@ref sch 13 para 2(b) (src:29035-29045)
GIVEN figures IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` MEANS
    (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` figures THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` figures THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` figures THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- "any 2 of the following criteria": at least 2 of the 3 (two or all three).
@ref sch 13 para 2(b) (src:29035-29045)
GIVEN figures IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` MEANS
    `sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` figures AT LEAST 2

§ `Paragraph 2: a company that has had 2 financial years before this one`

-- (a) a private company throughout the financial year; and (b) any 2 of the criteria for each of the 2 financial years immediately preceding.
-- "A company is a small company from a financial year if": an "if" gate, a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1).
-- src:29031 | 2. A company is a small company from a financial year if —
-- src:29033 | (a) it is a private company throughout the financial year; and
-- src:29035 | (b) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 financial
-- src:29036 | years immediately preceding the financial year:
-- src:29038 | (i) the revenue of the company for each financial year does not
-- src:29039 | exceed $10 million;
-- src:29041 | (ii) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of each
-- src:29042 | financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29044 | (iii) it has at the end of each financial year not more than
-- src:29045 | 50 employees.
@ref sch 13 para 2 (src:29031-29045)
GIVEN `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` MEANS
    IF     `the company is a private company throughout the financial year`
       AND `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`
       AND `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is a small company from a financial year if -- (a) it is a private company throughout the financial year; and (b) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 financial years immediately preceding the financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork lines F-S1 and F-M1)

-- OTHER READING (B), not called by anything else: the SAME two criteria must be satisfied in both preceding years ("(i) the revenue of the company for
-- each financial year does not exceed ..." read as holding in both years). Fork line F-S1.
@ref sch 13 para 2 (src:29031-29045)
GIVEN `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 2(b) the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year (other reading: the same 2 criteria in both years)` MEANS
    IF     `the company is a private company throughout the financial year`
       AND (      (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` AND `sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` `the figures of the financial year before that` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
            PLUS (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` AND `sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` `the figures of the financial year before that` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
            PLUS (IF `sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` AND `sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` `the figures of the financial year before that` THEN 1 ELSE 0)) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the same "if" gate as paragraph 2, read as requiring the same 2 criteria in each year (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a))

§ `Paragraph 3: a company that has not reached its third financial year after incorporation`

-- "Despite paragraph 2, where a company has not reached its third financial year after incorporation, a company is a small company (a) from its first financial
-- year after incorporation if (i) it is a private company throughout its first financial year; and (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the criteria for its first financial year;
-- or (b) from its second financial year after incorporation if ... its second financial year". The financial year asked about is the first or the second.
-- A company that has reached its third financial year is outside the paragraph: NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)).
-- src:29047 | 3. Despite paragraph 2, where a company has not reached its third financial year
-- src:29048 | after incorporation, a company is a small company —
-- src:29050 | (a) from its first financial year after incorporation if —
-- src:29052 | (i) it is a private company throughout its first financial year; and
-- src:29054 | (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for its first financial
-- src:29055 | year:
-- src:29057 | (A) the revenue of the company for its first financial year
-- src:29058 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29060 | (B) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of its
-- src:29061 | first financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29063 | (C) it has at the end of its first financial year not more than
-- src:29064 | 50 employees; or
-- src:29071 | (b) from its second financial year after incorporation if —
-- src:29073 | (i) it is a private company throughout its second financial year;
-- src:29074 | and
-- src:29076 | (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for its second
-- src:29077 | financial year:
-- src:29079 | (A) the revenue of the company for its second financial year
-- src:29080 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29082 | (B) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of its
-- src:29083 | second financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29085 | (C) it has at the end of its second financial year not more than
-- src:29086 | 50 employees.
@ref sch 13 para 3 (src:29047-29086)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` EQUALS 1 OR `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` EQUALS 2
    THEN (IF `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` AND `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is a small company (a) from its first financial year after incorporation if (i) it is a private company throughout its first financial year; and (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for its first financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a company has not reached its third financial year after incorporation" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)); the paragraph says nothing of a company that has reached it (paragraph 2 does)

§ `Paragraph 4: a company incorporated before 1 July 2015`

-- "Despite paragraph 2, a company which was incorporated before 1 July 2015 is a small company (a) from the first financial year that commences on or after
-- 1 July 2015 if ... (b) from the second financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015 if ...". The number asked counts the financial years that commence on
-- or after 1 July 2015, the first as 1. A company incorporated on or after that day, or in a later financial year: outside the paragraph, NOTHING (item (c)).
-- src:29088 | 4. Despite paragraph 2, a company which was incorporated before 1 July 2015 is
-- src:29089 | a small company —
-- src:29091 | (a) from the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015
-- src:29092 | if —
-- src:29094 | (i) it is a private company throughout the first financial year; and
-- src:29096 | (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the first financial
-- src:29097 | year:
-- src:29099 | (A) the revenue of the company for the first financial year
-- src:29100 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29102 | (B) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of the
-- src:29103 | first financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29105 | (C) it has at the end of the first financial year not more than
-- src:29106 | 50 employees; or
-- src:29108 | (b) from the second financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015
-- src:29109 | if —
-- src:29111 | (i) it is a private company throughout the second financial year;
-- src:29112 | and
-- src:29114 | (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the second
-- src:29115 | financial year:
-- src:29117 | (A) the revenue of the company for the second financial year
-- src:29118 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29120 | (B) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of the
-- src:29121 | second financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29128 | (C) it has at the end of the second financial year not more than
-- src:29129 | 50 employees.
@ref sch 13 para 4 (src:29088-29129)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` MEANS
    IF     `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `sch 13 the day 1 July 2015`
       AND (`the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS 1 OR `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS 2)
    THEN (IF `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` AND `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company which was incorporated before 1 July 2015 is a small company (a) from the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015 if (i) it is a private company throughout the first financial year; and (ii) it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the first financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company which was incorporated before 1 July 2015" and the first or second financial year that commences on or after that day are scope limits with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

§ `Paragraphs 5 and 6: when a small company ceases to be one`

-- Paragraph 6: "Paragraph 5 does not apply (a) to a company that has not reached its third financial year after incorporation; or (b) in the case of a company that was incorporated
-- before 1 July 2015, to a company that has not reached its third financial year after that date." A flat negative for the cases it lists; the list is not closed with "only",
-- so outside it the paragraph says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:29150 | 6. Paragraph 5 does not apply —
-- src:29152 | (a) to a company that has not reached its third financial year after
-- src:29153 | incorporation; or
-- src:29155 | (b) in the case of a company that was incorporated before 1 July 2015, to a
-- src:29156 | company that has not reached its third financial year after that date.
@ref sch 13 para 6 (src:29150-29156)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` MEANS
    IF     `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` AT MOST 2
        OR (    `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `sch 13 the day 1 July 2015`
            AND `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` AT MOST 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Paragraph 5 does not apply (a) to a company that has not reached its third financial year after incorporation; or (b) ..." lists two cases without "only", and says nothing of any other (paragraph 5 itself answers)

-- Paragraph 5: "Subject to paragraph 6, a small company ceases to be a small company from a financial year if (a) it ceases to be a private company at any time during the
-- financial year; or (b) it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 consecutive financial years immediately preceding the financial year".
-- (C1): (b) is met where, in EACH of the two years, fewer than 2 criteria hold. A company that was not small for the preceding financial year has nothing to cease: NOTHING.
-- src:29131 | 5. Subject to paragraph 6, a small company ceases to be a small company from a
-- src:29132 | financial year if —
-- src:29134 | (a) it ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year;
-- src:29135 | or
-- src:29137 | (b) it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for each of the
-- src:29138 | 2 consecutive financial years immediately preceding the financial
-- src:29139 | year:
-- src:29141 | (i) the revenue of the company for each financial year does not
-- src:29142 | exceed $10 million;
-- src:29144 | (ii) the value of the company’s total assets at the end of each
-- src:29145 | financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29147 | (iii) it has at the end of each financial year not more than
-- src:29148 | 50 employees.
@ref sch 13 para 5 (src:29131-29148)
GIVEN `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a small company ceases to be a small company" speaks of a company that is small; the paragraph says nothing of one that is not
    ELSE (IF `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` `the date the company was incorporated` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 5 does not apply (a) to a company that has not reached its third financial year after incorporation; or (b) in the case of a company that was incorporated before 1 July 2015, to a company that has not reached its third financial year after that date" (a flat negative)
          ELSE (IF     `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year`
                    OR (    (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`))
                        AND (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`)))
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a small company ceases to be a small company from a financial year if (a) it ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year; or (b) it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 consecutive financial years immediately preceding the financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork lines F-S2 and F-M1)

-- OTHER READING (C2), not called by anything else: the company ceases where it fails to satisfy any 2 criteria in EITHER of the 2 preceding years. Fork line F-S2.
@ref sch 13 para 5 (src:29131-29148)
GIVEN `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 5(b) the company fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` MEANS
       (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`))
    OR (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`))

§ `Paragraph 1(a) and paragraph 13(a): is the company a small company for the financial year`

-- "a company is a small company if it qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2, 3 or 4, whichever may be applicable, and the company continues to be a small company
-- until it ceases to be a small company under paragraph 5" (paragraph 1(a)); a reference to a company being a small company from a financial year means that it is one for that year
-- and every later year until it ceases under paragraph 5 (paragraph 13(a)). So: the company is small for the year if it qualifies under 2, 3 or 4 for it, or it was small for the year
-- before and does not cease under paragraph 5. s 205C(5) hands the meaning of "small company" to the Schedule: when no head holds the answer is JUST FALSE
-- (the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)).
-- src:29019 | 1. For the purposes of section 205C —
-- src:29021 | (a) a company is a small company if it qualifies as a small company under
-- src:29022 | paragraph 2, 3 or 4, whichever may be applicable, and the company
-- src:29023 | continues to be a small company until it ceases to be a small company
-- src:29024 | under paragraph 5; and
@ref sch 13 para 1(a) (src:29019-29024)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` MEANS
    IF     (`qualifies under paragraph 2` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`qualifies under paragraph 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`qualifies under paragraph 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` AND (NOT (`ceases under paragraph 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is a small company if it qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2, 3 or 4, whichever may be applicable, and the company continues to be a small company until it ceases to be a small company under paragraph 5" (a definition handed to the Schedule by s 205C(5): the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a): no head holds)
    WHERE
        `qualifies under paragraph 2` MEANS `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` `the figures of the financial year before that`
        `qualifies under paragraph 3` MEANS `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` `the figures of the financial year`
        `qualifies under paragraph 4` MEANS `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` `the date the company was incorporated` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` `the figures of the financial year`
        `ceases under paragraph 5` MEANS `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year` `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` `the date the company was incorporated` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` `the figures of the financial year before that`

-- src:29282 | 13. For the purposes of this Schedule —
-- src:29284 | (a) a reference to a company being a small company from a financial year
-- src:29285 | means that the company is a small company for that financial year and
-- src:29286 | every subsequent financial year until it ceases to be a small company
-- src:29287 | under paragraph 5;
@ref sch 13 para 13(a) (src:29282-29287)
GIVEN `the company is a small company from an earlier financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ceased to be a small company under paragraph 5 since then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 13(a) the company is a small company for the later financial year` MEANS
    IF `the company is a small company from an earlier financial year`
    THEN (IF `the company has ceased to be a small company under paragraph 5 since then`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is a small company for that financial year and every subsequent financial year until it ceases to be a small company under paragraph 5" (an "until" bar)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 13(a) explains what "a small company from a financial year" means and says nothing of a company that is not one

-- src:29299 | 14. To avoid doubt —
-- src:29301 | (a) a company that has ceased to be a small company under
-- src:29302 | paragraph 5 may become a small company again if it subsequently
-- src:29303 | qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2; and
@ref sch 13 para 14(a) (src:29299-29303)
GIVEN `the company has ceased to be a small company under paragraph 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company subsequently qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 14(a) the company may become a small company again` MEANS
    IF `the company has ceased to be a small company under paragraph 5` AND `the company subsequently qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To avoid doubt -- a company that has ceased to be a small company under paragraph 5 may become a small company again if it subsequently qualifies as a small company under paragraph 2" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

§ `Paragraphs 7 to 11: the small group`

-- Paragraph 7(a) to (c): the same three criteria on the group's consolidated revenue, consolidated total assets and aggregate employees ("the consolidated revenue of the group for each
-- financial year does not exceed $10 million; the value of the consolidated total assets ... does not exceed $10 million; the group has ... an aggregate number of employees of not more than 50").
-- The thresholds are paragraph 2(b)'s; the figures here are the group's.
-- src:29158 | 7. A group is a small group from a financial year if the group satisfies any 2 of
-- src:29159 | the following criteria for each of the 2 consecutive financial years immediately
-- src:29160 | preceding the financial year:
-- src:29162 | (a) the consolidated revenue of the group for each financial year does not
-- src:29163 | exceed $10 million;
-- src:29165 | (b) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end of each
-- src:29166 | financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29168 | (c) the group has at the end of each financial year an aggregate number of
-- src:29169 | employees of not more than 50.
@ref sch 13 para 7 (src:29158-29169)
GIVEN `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 7 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` MEANS
    IF     `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`
       AND `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A group is a small group from a financial year if the group satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for each of the 2 consecutive financial years immediately preceding the financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork lines F-S1 and F-M1)

-- src:29171 | 8. Despite paragraph 7, a group is a small group —
-- src:29173 | (a) from its first financial year after it is formed if it satisfies any 2 of the
-- src:29174 | following criteria for its first financial year:
-- src:29176 | (i) the consolidated revenue of the group for its first financial year
-- src:29177 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29184 | (ii) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end
-- src:29185 | of its first financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29187 | (iii) the group has at the end of its first financial year an aggregate
-- src:29188 | number of employees of not more than 50; or
-- src:29190 | (b) from its second financial year after it is formed if it satisfies any 2 of
-- src:29191 | the following criteria for its second financial year:
-- src:29193 | (i) the consolidated revenue of the group for its second financial
-- src:29194 | year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29196 | (ii) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end
-- src:29197 | of its second financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29199 | (iii) the group has at the end of its second financial year an
-- src:29200 | aggregate number of employees of not more than 50.
@ref sch 13 para 8 (src:29171-29200)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 8 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` EQUALS 1 OR `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` EQUALS 2
    THEN (IF `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite paragraph 7, a group is a small group (a) from its first financial year after it is formed if it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for its first financial year; or (b) from its second financial year after it is formed if it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for its second financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 8 names the first and the second financial year after the group is formed and says nothing of a later one (paragraph 7 answers)

-- src:29202 | 9. Despite paragraph 7, a group which is formed before 1 July 2015 is a small
-- src:29203 | group —
-- src:29205 | (a) from the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015, if
-- src:29206 | it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the first financial year:
-- src:29208 | (i) the consolidated revenue of the group for the first financial year
-- src:29209 | does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29211 | (ii) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end
-- src:29212 | of the first financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29214 | (iii) the group has at the end of the first financial year an aggregate
-- src:29215 | number of employees of not more than 50; or
-- src:29217 | (b) from the second financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015
-- src:29218 | if it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the second financial
-- src:29219 | year:
-- src:29221 | (i) the consolidated revenue of the group for the second financial
-- src:29222 | year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29224 | (ii) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end
-- src:29225 | of the second financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29227 | (iii) the group has at the end of the second financial year an
-- src:29228 | aggregate number of employees of not more than 50.
@ref sch 13 para 9 (src:29202-29228)
GIVEN `the date the group was formed` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` MEANS
    IF     `the date the group was formed` LESS THAN `sch 13 the day 1 July 2015`
       AND (`the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS 1 OR `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS 2)
    THEN (IF `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite paragraph 7, a group which is formed before 1 July 2015 is a small group (a) from the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015, if it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the first financial year; or (b) from the second financial year ... if it satisfies any 2 of the following criteria for the second financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a group which is formed before 1 July 2015" and the first or second financial year that commences on or after that day are scope limits with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- Paragraph 11: "Paragraph 10 does not apply (a) to a group that has not reached its third financial year after it is formed; or (b) in the case of a group that was formed before 1 July 2015, to a group that has not reached its third financial year after that date."
-- src:29248 | 11. Paragraph 10 does not apply —
-- src:29250 | (a) to a group that has not reached its third financial year after it is formed;
-- src:29251 | or
-- src:29253 | (b) in the case of a group that was formed before 1 July 2015, to a group
-- src:29254 | that has not reached its third financial year after that date.
@ref sch 13 para 11 (src:29248-29254)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the group was formed` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` MEANS
    IF     `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` AT MOST 2
        OR (    `the date the group was formed` LESS THAN `sch 13 the day 1 July 2015`
            AND `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` AT MOST 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Paragraph 10 does not apply (a) to a group that has not reached its third financial year after it is formed; or (b) ..." lists two cases without "only"

-- Paragraph 10: "Subject to paragraph 11, a small group ceases to be a small group from a financial year if it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for 2 consecutive financial years
-- immediately preceding the financial year" (C1: fewer than 2 criteria hold in EACH of the two years).
-- src:29230 | 10. Subject to paragraph 11, a small group ceases to be a small group from a
-- src:29231 | financial year if it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for 2 consecutive
-- src:29232 | financial years immediately preceding the financial year:
-- src:29239 | (a) the consolidated revenue of the group for each financial year does not
-- src:29240 | exceed $10 million;
-- src:29242 | (b) the value of the consolidated total assets of the group at the end of each
-- src:29243 | financial year does not exceed $10 million;
-- src:29245 | (c) the group has at the end of each financial year an aggregate number of
-- src:29246 | employees of not more than 50.
@ref sch 13 para 10 (src:29230-29246)
GIVEN `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the group was formed` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` MEANS
    IF NOT `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a small group ceases to be a small group" speaks of a group that is small; the paragraph says nothing of one that is not
    ELSE (IF `sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` `the date the group was formed` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 10 does not apply (a) to a group that has not reached its third financial year after it is formed; or (b) ..." (a flat negative)
          ELSE (IF     (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`))
                   AND (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`))
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a small group ceases to be a small group from a financial year if it does not satisfy any 2 of the following criteria for 2 consecutive financial years immediately preceding the financial year" (an "if" gate: marginal reading (a), fork lines F-S2 and F-M1)

-- OTHER READING (C2), not called by anything else: the group ceases where it fails to satisfy any 2 criteria in EITHER of the 2 preceding years. Fork line F-S2.
@ref sch 13 para 10 (src:29230-29246)
GIVEN `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 10 the group fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` MEANS
       (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding`))
    OR (NOT (`sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `the figures of the financial year before that`))

-- src:29026 | (b) a group is a small group if it qualifies as a small group under
-- src:29027 | paragraph 7, 8 or 9, whichever may be applicable, and the group
-- src:29028 | continues to be a small group until it ceases to be a small group under
-- src:29029 | paragraph 10.
@ref sch 13 para 1(b) (src:29026-29029)
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the group was formed` IS A DATE
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figures of the financial year` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
      `the figures of the financial year before that` IS A `sch 13 year figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` MEANS
    IF     (`qualifies under paragraph 7` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`qualifies under paragraph 8` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`qualifies under paragraph 9` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` AND (NOT (`ceases under paragraph 10` EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a group is a small group if it qualifies as a small group under paragraph 7, 8 or 9, whichever may be applicable, and the group continues to be a small group until it ceases to be a small group under paragraph 10" (a definition handed to the Schedule by s 205C(5): the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a): no head holds)
    WHERE
        `qualifies under paragraph 7` MEANS `sch 13 para 7 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` `the figures of the financial year before that`
        `qualifies under paragraph 8` MEANS `sch 13 para 8 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` `the figures of the financial year`
        `qualifies under paragraph 9` MEANS `sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `the date the group was formed` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the figures of the financial year`
        `ceases under paragraph 10` MEANS `sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` `the date the group was formed` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the figures of the financial year immediately preceding` `the figures of the financial year before that`

§ `Paragraphs 12 to 14: what the Schedule says about groups, the parent, and a return to being small`

-- 12(a): whether an entity is part of a group is decided in accordance with the Accounting Standards (not among the sources): the fact is supplied.
-- src:29256 | 12. For the purposes of this Schedule —
-- src:29258 | (a) the question whether an entity is part of a group is to be decided in
-- src:29259 | accordance with the Accounting Standards;
@ref sch 13 para 12(a) (src:29256-29259)
GIVEN `the entity is part of a group within the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 12(a) the entity is part of the group` MEANS
    IF `the entity is part of a group within the Accounting Standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the question whether an entity is part of a group is to be decided in accordance with the Accounting Standards" (a question handed to the Accounting Standards, which are not among the sources: the fact is supplied)

-- 12(b)(i): where consolidated financial statements are prepared by a parent, the group's consolidated total assets and consolidated revenue are determined in accordance with the accounting
-- standards applicable to the group (the figure is supplied); (ii) where they are not prepared, each is the aggregate of all the members of the group.
-- src:29261 | (b) in the case —
-- src:29263 | (i) where consolidated financial statements are prepared by a
-- src:29264 | parent in relation to a group, the “consolidated total assets” and
-- src:29265 | “consolidated revenue” of the group are to be determined in
-- src:29266 | accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the
-- src:29267 | group; or
-- src:29269 | (ii) where consolidated financial statements are not prepared by a
-- src:29270 | parent in relation to a group —
-- src:29272 | (A) “consolidated total assets” means the aggregate total
-- src:29273 | assets of all the members of the group; and
-- src:29275 | (B) “consolidated revenue” means the aggregate revenue of
-- src:29276 | all the members of the group; and
@ref sch 13 para 12(b) (src:29261-29276)
GIVEN `consolidated financial statements are prepared by a parent in relation to the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated total assets of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the total assets of each member of the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated total assets of the group, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `consolidated financial statements are prepared by a parent in relation to the group`
    THEN `the consolidated total assets of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE sum `the total assets of each member of the group, in Singapore dollars`

@ref sch 13 para 12(b) (src:29261-29276)
GIVEN `consolidated financial statements are prepared by a parent in relation to the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated revenue of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the revenue of each member of the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated revenue of the group, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `consolidated financial statements are prepared by a parent in relation to the group`
    THEN `the consolidated revenue of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE sum `the revenue of each member of the group, in Singapore dollars`

-- src:29278 | (c) “parent” has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards, but does
-- src:29279 | not include any entity which is a subsidiary of any other entity within
-- src:29280 | the meaning of the Accounting Standards.
@ref sch 13 para 12(c) (src:29278-29280)
GIVEN `the entity is a parent within the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a subsidiary of any other entity within the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 12(c) the entity is a parent for the purposes of the Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the entity is a parent within the Accounting Standards` AND (NOT `the entity is a subsidiary of any other entity within the Accounting Standards`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'parent' has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards, but does not include any entity which is a subsidiary of any other entity within the meaning of the Accounting Standards" (a closed meaning with an express exclusion)

-- src:29294 | (b) a reference to a group being a small group from a financial year means
-- src:29295 | that the group is a small group for that financial year and every
-- src:29296 | subsequent financial year until it ceases to be a small group under
-- src:29297 | paragraph 10.
@ref sch 13 para 13(b) (src:29294-29297)
GIVEN `the group is a small group from an earlier financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10 since then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 13(b) the group is a small group for the later financial year` MEANS
    IF `the group is a small group from an earlier financial year`
    THEN (IF `the group has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10 since then`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the group is a small group for that financial year and every subsequent financial year until it ceases to be a small group under paragraph 10" (an "until" bar)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 13(b) explains what "a small group from a financial year" means and says nothing of a group that is not one

-- src:29305 | (b) a group that has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10 may
-- src:29306 | become a small group again if it subsequently qualifies as a small
-- src:29307 | group under paragraph 7.
@ref sch 13 para 14(b) (src:29305-29307)
GIVEN `the group has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group subsequently qualifies as a small group under paragraph 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 14(b) the group may become a small group again` MEANS
    IF `the group has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10` AND `the group subsequently qualifies as a small group under paragraph 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a group that has ceased to be a small group under paragraph 10 may become a small group again if it subsequently qualifies as a small group under paragraph 7" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)
